--- CORRECTION NOTE (added 2026-10-22 after FRICK-REVIEW-0426/0427) ---
  The script above labels offset 0x08 as 'TIME' and 0x04 as 'STATUS'. Per the cited public
  register map these are STATUS (0x08) and CONTROL (0x04); TIME is 0x0c and was never probed. The
  observations must therefore be read as:
    - 0x08 (STATUS): 0x00000000 initially, 0x00000010 after the first write to 0x08
      (bit 4 = LOCKED per the header's MSS_WDOG_LOCKED), constant 0x00000010 afterwards;
    - 0x04 (CONTROL): constant 0x00000002 (never written by the probe);
    - 0x14 (TRIGGER): re-write after configuration read back 0x0000000A (the re-write took effect);
      writing 0x1000 gave 'Unhandled bits: [12]' and read back 0x00000000 (12-bit field);
    - the 'Unhandled bits' warnings on offset 0x8 are STATUS-register warnings (bits 5-7 are
      unimplemented in the model; one carries 'Tags: DEVRST (0x1)'), NOT TIME-width evidence;
    - the TIME register (0x0c) was never read: no statement about the model's TIME width is
      established by this probe;
    - the wrong-key and correct-key REFRESH writes were not in the same model state (the counter
      was not running and REFRESH was never read back), so the probe does NOT establish that the
      model lacks a key-sensitive observable.
